    "note": "Dominant identifier strings contain secured-debt instrument text plus reference-rate spread, PIK terms, floor, and maturity date. Spread values are stated as bps after the reference rate, e.g. SOFR+200 means 2.00%. Identifier datapoints present include industry/sector, issuer/borrower, instrument type, tranche/facility type, reference rate, spread, PIK wording, floor, and maturity. Par/fair-value/source-table columns are not treated as identifier datapoints."
